    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Rare</em></p><p>This Tiny cube looks like a jack-in-the-box. When you turn its crank as a Magic action, it plays a cheerful tune, its lid pops open, a creature appears in the nearest unoccupied space, and the lid shuts again. The lid can’t be opened any other way.</p><p>Roll on the Cube of Summoning table to find out which spell the cube casts to summon the creature. The spell is cast at level 5 (save DC 17, +9 attack bonus) and doesn’t require Concentration, but you otherwise act as the spell’s caster.</p><p>Once the cube has summoned a creature, it can’t do so again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Cube of Summoning</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th>1d6</th><th>Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Summon Aberration</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Summon Beast</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Summon Construct</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSummonDrag]{Summon Dragon}</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Summon Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Summon Fey</td></tr></tbody></table><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-KZwwjwHHZVyeijWF\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Turn the Crank</em> dépense l’utilisation du jour et lance la table ; utilisez ensuite l’activité du sort obtenu. Seul <em>Summon Dragon</em> existe dans dnd5e : les autres activités <em>Cast</em> sont vides, déposez-y le sort si vous l’avez.</p></section>",
